        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> For the textobject `v = { \"⟨.-⟩\", \"^.().*().$\" }` and the text `⟨abc⟩`, positioning the cursor on the `b` and pressing `div` will delete the entire string.\r\n\r\nThis is because both \"⟨\" and \"⟩\" are multibyte characters, while \".\" in Lua pattern matches a single byte character. Using `{ '⟨.-⟩', '^⟨().*()⟩$' }` as specification should solve this.",
